# Cursor / other-agent entry point
#
# The canonical rules live in AGENTS.md. Read that file first; this file only
# mirrors the non-negotiables so editors that look for .cursorrules still see
# them.

Read and obey `AGENTS.md` and everything under `docs/` before writing code.

Hard rules:

- No `.unwrap()` / `.expect()` in handlers, services, or extractors.
- No SQL in handlers; `sqlx` never appears in `handlers.rs`.
- Every money/credit mutation runs in one PostgreSQL transaction with its
  ledger row.
- Never expose S3 keys — only `presign_get` URLs leave the API.
- Service order status changes only through the service layer with
  `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`; illegal transitions return `409`.
- Frontend: `<script setup lang="ts">`, all HTTP via `src/api/client.ts`,
  colours via CSS tokens only, no CDN fonts.
- Font is `Anek Bangla Variable`, self-hosted in `assets/fonts/anek-bangla/`.
- Migrations are append-only: add `000N_*.sql`, never edit an applied one.
- Commits are topic-scoped Conventional Commits (e.g. `feat(auth): ...`).
- **Anti-bloat rules live in `AGENTS.md` §9 and are binding.** Write the
  minimum code the spec needs; no repository layer, no speculative traits, no
  new crate/config flag without asking. Do not copy those rules here — one
  source of truth.

Full specification index: see `AGENTS.md` section 1.
